meta {
  name: Write game notes
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/games/{{gameId}}/note
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "body": "Left off in the Fire Temple, need the second key.\n\nTodo: sword upgrade before Ganon."
  }
}

docs {
  Replace the notes on one of the caller's games.

  PUT rather than PATCH because there is one field and it replaces outright: no
  "leave unchanged" state exists for omission to express. Separate from
  PATCH /me/games/{id} because that route answers with a whole GameRead, which
  notes stay off by design.

  A blank (or whitespace-only) body DELETES the note row rather than storing an
  empty string, so "no note" has a single representation and a cleared note cannot
  come back carrying a timestamp implying something was written.

  - 200 the saved note `{ body, updatedAt }`
  - 404 no such game in the caller's library
  - 422 over 20,000 characters, or an unknown key
  - 429 over the write budget
}
